-       An inline given, for any type `Instantiable across Paths from Text`: `val git: Path on
-       Linux = sh"which git"()` reads the trimmed output as a path, through the `Computable`
-       instance for path types. The type must be fixed by the expected type, since the
-       command alone cannot choose it.
+     detail
+         Un given inline, pour tout type `Instantiable across Paths from Text` : `val git: Path on
+         Linux = sh"which git"()` lit la sortie élaguée comme un chemin, via l'instance
+         `Computable` des types de chemin. Le type doit être fixé par le type attendu, puisque la
+         commande seule ne peut pas le choisir.

- entry .Parameterizable   how a value of a type is rendered as a command argument in `sh"…"`
+ entry .Parameterizable
+   info
+       la façon dont une valeur d'un type est rendue comme argument de commande dans `sh"…"`

-   detail
-       `T is Parameterizable` lets a `T` be substituted into the `sh"…"` interpolator:
-       `#show` renders it as the text of one argument, which the interpolator then escapes for
-       its position, so the instance never concerns itself with quoting. The companion's
-       `.encodable` covers every type `Encodable in Text` — a `Path`, a URL, a `Pid` — and a
-       type with neither is a compile error at the substitution. `Text`, `List[Text]` and
-       `Command` substitute through their own `Sh` insertions rather than this.
+   detail
+       `T is Parameterizable` permet de substituer un `T` dans l'interpolateur `sh"…"` : `#show`
+       le rend sous forme du texte d'un argument, que l'interpolateur échappe ensuite selon sa
+       position, de sorte que l'instance n'a jamais à se soucier des guillemets. Le `.encodable`
+       du compagnon couvre tout type `Encodable in Text` — un `Path`, une URL, un `Pid` — et un
+       type qui n'a ni l'un ni l'autre est une erreur de compilation à la substitution. `Text`,
+       `List[Text]` et `Command` se substituent par leurs propres insertions `Sh` plutôt que par
+       ceci.

=       `Command` substitute through their own `Sh` insertions rather than this.
=
-       ```scala
+       ```scala

=       `Command` substitute through their own `Sh` insertions rather than this.
=
=       ```scala
-       import soundness.*
+       import soundness.*

-       case class Tag(value: Int)
+       case class Tag(value: Int)

-       given Tag is Parameterizable = summon[Text is Parameterizable].contramap(tag => t"<${tag.value}>")
+       given Tag is Parameterizable = summon[Text is Parameterizable].contramap(tag => t"<${tag.value}>")

-       sh"echo ${Tag(7)}"   // Command(t"echo", t"<7>")
+       sh"echo ${Tag(7)}"   // Command(t"echo", t"<7>")

=       sh"echo ${Tag(7)}"   // Command(t"echo", t"<7>")
-       ```
+       ```

=       ```
